// twinspeak.rc -- v6.6.4: app icon + version info. v7.5.4: version bump
// (the uniform sheet row: the ACTIVE row joins the INACTIVE byte --
// Gdiplus::Color(128,43,43,43), the field's pick -- so no alpha-0 row exists
// anywhere and the minimize glass flash is impossible by construction; and
// the fake top border bar engine -- the row constants, the byte-direct
// patch, the row-first commit, the NC latch, the gate, the kick and the
// fade presenter thread -- moves into customWindow.h behind the API:
// cwSeedSheetRow, cwPatchSheetRow, cwCommitSheetRowFast, cwSheetRowGate,
// cwSheetRowKick, cwSheetRowLatch/cwSheetRowLatchValue,
// cwSheetPresenterStart/Stop. v7.5.2: version bump
// (the one-file window: customWindow.h arrives -- the whole Windows chrome
// (WM_NCCALCSIZE insets, WM_NCHITTEST, the caption button stack, the hover,
// the sysmenu, the face/title/icon/button painting, the built-in fallback
// tray, putWindowinTray) moves behind an eleven-function API:
// enableCustomWin, changeWinTitlebarColor, changeWinTextColor,
// changeWinTextUnfocusedColor, changeWinTextFont, enableWinIcon,
// setWinTitlebarButtonLayout, setCanWinResize, changeWinMinimizeHoverColor,
// changeWinMaximizeHoverColor, putWindowinTray -- Windows-real with no-op
// stubs for every other target. twinspeak stays consumer #1, byte-identical:
// applyTheme re-seeds the chrome from the live theme, guiRenderBar keeps the
// sheet row + edge sandwich, guiWndProc forwards through cwWndProc first.
// v7.4.11: version bump
// (the forced replay: the tray-icon come-up -- tray click, tray menu,
// second-instance come-up -- now runs the same second activation the plain
// start runs, FORCED past its foreground guard: the click on the tray icon
// grants the foreground to the tray (Explorer) and this process holds no
// grant of its own, so the guard-only replay exited every time and the
// button waited for a manual unfocus + refocus. Forced, the replay takes
// the foreground with the v7.4.8 attach dance -- the user asked for this
// window -- then runs the blip unchanged. Plain start stays byte for byte
// v7.4.10: unforced arm, guard intact. v7.4.10: version bump
// (the plain process + the second activation: the v7.1.23 process
// AppUserModelID is RETIRED too -- the panel window has been vanilla since
// v7.4.9 but the process still carried the AUMID, so every button was
// still born into the AUMID group's lifecycle instead of the plain window
// path, with the windowless sign-in --tray twin as the group's claimant;
// grouping, jumplist, balloons and the label all run on the default path
// now. And tsReplayActivation replays the field machine's one proven
// birth trigger -- the user's own unfocus + refocus pair -- ~500 ms after
// every first show: a 1x1 off-screen toolwindow proxy takes the
// foreground for 40 ms and hands it straight back, only while the panel
// still owns the foreground. v7.4.9: version bump
// (the vanilla window + the name-change channel: the per-window
// System.AppUserModel.ID property (v7.1.25) is retired -- it never fixed
// what it was added for and it routed the labeled taskbar's button birth
// out of the default window path; the panel is a vanilla window again and
// tsEnsureTaskbarButton now re-announces the window title (the
// EVENT_OBJECT_NAMECHANGE channel) immediately after every first show plus
// a 250 ms nag budget for the sign-in race. The double-clicked duplicate
// hands its foreground grant to the running instance before forwarding
// "come up" (AllowSetForegroundWindow). v7.4.8: version bump
// (the button audit: the activating show of v7.4.7 was still not enough --
// the taskbar button stayed unborn until an activation change. After every
// first show tsEnsureTaskbarButton now takes the foreground with the
// thread-input attach dance when the launch activation was suppressed and
// asserts WS_EX_APPWINDOW -- a button-worthiness style change on a channel
// that depends on neither the show nor the foreground event; a native
// button, not an ITaskbarList tab. v7.4.7: version bump
// (the button ride: a plain launch showed the panel with SW_SHOWNA -- a
// no-activate show -- and the taskbar button stayed unborn until an
// activation change (the field: "'TidyVision TwinSpeak' will not show up
// anywhere on the taskbar until I unfocus and refocus the window"). The
// first show is ShowWindow(SW_SHOW) now: show AND activate in one shell
// transaction, the transaction the button birth rides. v7.4.6: version bump
// (the legacy shadow, retired: the class carried CS_DROPSHADOW next to the
// DWM shadow -- win32k's legacy shadow is a separate "SysShadow" sprite
// drawn OFFSET DOWN-RIGHT of the owner window, and its show/hide lifecycle
// around a hide-to-tray + reopen cycle is exactly where the tray-reopen
// ghost came from; the v7.4.4 frame nudge re-anchored the sprite, the
// v7.4.5 sheet re-commit cannot touch it. CS_DROPSHADOW is gone from the
// class style -- no SysShadow window can exist, no ghost can. The
// Windows-default shadow stays: WS_THICKFRAME + the default border color
// + the glass sheet own it under composition. Also in v7.4.6: a plain
// (no --tray) launch adds the tray icon at startup -- it used to ride the
// first close-to-tray. v7.4.5: version bump
// (the sheet re-commit: the v7.4.4 frame-change nudge recomputes the
// win32 side of the frame but DWM's own shadow projection can still
// resurrect stale -- the right/bottom tray-reopen ghost; guiRestoreWindow
// re-commits the glass sheet after the nudge, RAD-style, twice --
// {0,0,0,0} then the real {0,0,1,0} -- so DWM cannot filter the unchanged
// margins and must rebuild frame + shadow against the live rect. The
// settled state is the exact v7.1.27 sheet. v7.4.4: version bump
// (the shadow rebuild: SW_HIDE retires the window's DWM visual and SW_SHOW
// rebuilds it from cached frame metadata -- the drop shadow lands at the
// stale bounds, detached from the real rect on tray reopen;
// guiRestoreWindow fires the WM_CREATE nudge (v7.1.24, RAD main.c) once per
// restore -- SWP_FRAMECHANGED|NOMOVE|NOSIZE|NOZORDER|NOACTIVATE, geometry
// only, the glass sheet and the recipe rows untouched. v7.4.3: version bump
// (the inactive row, the field's gray: kSheetRowInactive 0x80000000 ->
// 0x802B2B2B -- BGRA(43,43,43,0x80), half-alpha RGB(43,43,43), the
// recipe's own source gray, now one pinned constant. v7.4.2: version bump
// (the inactive row, half-alpha black: kSheetRowInactive 0x80696969 ->
// 0x80000000 -- BGRA(0,0,0,0x80), the glass itself dimmed 50%, which is
// what the DWM's own inactive border is; a gray source byte dims AND
// tints. v7.4.1: version bump
// (the inactive row, pinned: on unfocus row 0 is the half-alpha #696969
// the classic inactive border rides -- the DWM's own recipe, composited
// by the same DWM over the same glass as the left/right/bottom strips --
// while the glass key BGRA(0,0,0,0) stays the active row. The v7.3.0
// backdrop estimator and the v7.3.2 hold latch are retired whole;
// v7.4.0's alpha-0-both-states row went BLACK on unfocus over a
// (252,252,252) backdrop -- the field's tape; Discord's custom-frame
// build carries the same hole). v7.3.2: version bump
// (the hold that does not expire: the deactivation hold is a LATCH --
// g_holdLive -- spanning the whole inactive period; the 240 ms
// wall-clock stamp, the clock checks in all three row writers and the
// presenter's handover present are retired -- the field caught the
// handover as "a transparency issue on the top border itself" and
// asked for the timer's head). v7.3.1: version bump
// (the row-first commit, the RAD
// contract: WM_NCACTIVATE lands the 1 px border row alone FIRST --
// guiCommitSheetRowFast -- before the full GDI+ face render, and answers
// the flip with DefWindowProcW's documented lParam -1, the RAD
// debugger's "without this result, stuff flickers").
// v7.3.0: version bump
// (the Chrome contract, tracked: on deactivation row 0 is OPAQUE at the
// settled recipe composite over the CURRENT backdrop -- computed live from
// the desktop strip above the window, v7.2.13's estimator -- stamped 240 ms
// and handed back to the recipe's half-alpha row by the fade presenter's
// own train [the stamp and the handover retired in v7.3.2]; DwmFlush() is
// back before the pre-flip present so a compose in flight can never carry
// the flip off a stale snapshot).
// v7.2.12: version bump
// (the hook thread goes quiet + the tray audit: the settle burst renders
// only when it must -- with a measured cache one tail tick replaces the
// twenty 50 Hz re-renders; the measure-retry tick is a bare re-measure;
// guiMeasureInstantRow reads the row with ONE BitBlt instead of up to 36
// GetPixel screen readbacks -- all on the GUI thread that answers the
// system-wide WH_MOUSE_LL hook, which is what the field felt as mouse
// lag; g_lastHealth rides its lock). Tray: the close-hint balloon works
// again (dead code since v7.1.20), the tooltip re-syncs after a delayed
// sign-in add, the icon loads at the tray's small size, TaskbarCreated is
// answered once by the owner window, the retry timer cannot orphan, and
// a tray-menu Start with unset devices says so in a balloon).
// v7.2.11: version bump
// (the latch answers for every path: the v7.2.9 NC latch moves into
// guiPaintBar, so no painter -- WM_PAINT, the bar hover paths, the
// settle-burst ticks, applyTheme -- can re-land the stale ACTIVE face and
// the alpha-0 bare-glass row in the transaction window between
// WM_NCACTIVATE and WM_ACTIVATE anymore; that stale face was the black
// caption + vanished top border the field's second tape catches on every
// unfocus). v7.2.10: version bump
// (the ever-seeded cache: the standalone seeder timer owns the initial
// g_instantInactive seed -- the burst-tail measure can lose the race against
// the quick-toggle test loop and the cache stayed empty for whole sessions,
// so every deactivation rode the DWM's transition and the top border
// flashed the pre-input blend until the second frame). v7.2.9: version bump
// (the one-frame row traced and killed: scan+median measure, NC-latched
// NCPAINT, symmetric activation present). v7.2.8: version bump
// (back to the 7.2.3 base + the post-flip NCPAINT). v7.2.3: version bump
// (the NC-flip present). v7.2.2: version bump
// + the name split: FileDescription stays the PROCESS name Task Manager
// reads ("TwinSpeak Control Panel"); ProductName takes the brand
// ("TidyVision TwinSpeak") -- the same split the windows carry (the taskbar
// window is "TidyVision TwinSpeak", the hidden tray surrogate is "TwinSpeak
// Control Panel").
// (v7.1.21: the manifest; v7.1.22..v7.2.0: window-side fixes only).
// No windows.h include needed -- the VERSIONINFO and
// RT_MANIFEST forms used here are RC syntax, not C macros, so both windres
// and zig rc accept this file as-is.
// v7.1.20: `1 24` embeds twinspeak.manifest (RT_MANIFEST = 24, id 1) --
// DPI awareness (the blur fix), comctl32 v6 (DarkMode_Explorer), asInvoker.
// v7.1.21: the manifest's XML comments lost their "--" (illegal inside XML
// comments -- the SxS loader refused the whole file and the exe would not
// start: "side-by-side configuration is incorrect").
1 ICON "twinspeak.ico"
1 24 "twinspeak.manifest"

1 VERSIONINFO
FILEVERSION     7,4,10,0
PRODUCTVERSION  7,4,10,0
FILEOS          0x40004L
FILETYPE        0x1L
FILESUBTYPE     0x0L
BEGIN
    BLOCK "StringFileInfo"
    BEGIN
        BLOCK "040904B0"
        BEGIN
            VALUE "CompanyName",      "TidyVision"
            VALUE "FileDescription",  "TwinSpeak Control Panel"
            VALUE "FileVersion",      "7.5.4.0"
            VALUE "InternalName",     "twinspeak"
            VALUE "LegalCopyright",   "Copyright 2026-beyond TidyVision -- MIT License"
            VALUE "OriginalFilename", "twinspeak.exe"
            VALUE "ProductName",      "TidyVision TwinSpeak"
            VALUE "ProductVersion",   "7.5.4.0"
        END
    END
    BLOCK "VarFileInfo"
    BEGIN
        VALUE "Translation", 0x409, 0x4B0
    END
END
